\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Evaluation inference protocol and budget}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{inference}

\p{An \strong{evaluation inference protocol} #{D} fixes the prompt wrapper,
decoder or search procedure, stopping rule, tool permissions, and aggregation
rule used at evaluation. Its \strong{budget} #{b} bounds declared resources
such as generated tokens, candidate rollouts, tool calls, or environment time.}

\p{For task #{q} and policy #{\pi}, let
#{\mathbb P^{D,b}_{q,\pi}} denote the probability law on completed evaluation
trajectories induced by the environment together with #{D} under budget
#{b}.}

\p{This is an FTIP synthesis. The pass-at-#{k} evaluations in
\citet{Section 5.1}{shao2024deepseekmath} and the base-versus-RL comparisons in
\citet{Sections 3--4}{yue2025does} vary sampling and evaluation procedures.
Naming #{D} and #{b} prevents a larger search budget from being reported as a
training gain.}

\p{The budget may be scalar for one controlled experiment. Cross-system work
should retain its components because one candidate rollout and one sandbox
minute are not equivalent resources.}
